course-assets/scenes/module-17/_logs/m17_L17_b09_slip-vs-pocket.png.log:3089:course-assets/scenes/module-17/_logs/m17_L17_b04_staircase.png.log:15:Generate one image with gpt-image-2 and save it to course-assets/scenes/module-17/m17_L17_b04_staircase.png (PNG, 1600x900). Match the attached style references and cast-board character style exactly. COMPOSITION: A chunky doodle staircase of four steps rising from left to right, drawn in cream and yellow. On the top step sits a neat stack of MONEY-GREEN bank-note bills (blank green notes, no writing) that is taller than a smaller green stack sitting on the second step — the money grows as the stairs rise. No people. Clean blue space upper-left for overlaid code text. STYLE: flat sticker-sheet doodle illustration, thick black hand-drawn outlines with a slight wobble, rounded corners, flat fills — palette is yellow, orange, cream, white, black on cornflower-blue #62b3f3, PLUS money-green used ONLY for cash / bank-notes (an intentional communication exception so money reads as money). No gradients, no texture, no shadows, no lighting, no perspective, no skin-tone shading. Faces use flat white/cream fill, tiny dot eyes, small subtle curved cast-board nose, simple mouth. Cylindrical limbs, strong simple silhouettes, confidently imperfect hand-drawn. No ambient doodles: no hearts, sparkles, notes, thought bubbles, motion marks, icons, random props, or decorative clutter. No text, letters, words, numbers, symbols, dollar signs, labels, captions, screens with writing, or readable paperwork anywhere. Leave clean open cornflower-blue space for code-rendered Sticker overlays. 16:9 composition, 1600x900 PNG.
