course-assets/scenes/module-17/_logs/m17_L17_b09_slip-vs-pocket.png.log:3516:docs/course-production/scripts/gen_carol_argue.sh:10:echo "Generate one image with gpt-image-2 and save it to $OUT/$FILE (PNG, 1600x900). Match the attached style references exactly. This is a TWO-PERSON scene. LEFT person = Carol, the SAME character as the attached portrait m02_L2B_carol.png — IDENTICAL face and build: a woman in her sixties, short curly LIGHT-GREY hair, ROUND GLASSES, cream shirt, pale near-white cream face; now looking FRUSTRATED and mid-argument, one hand raised gesturing, the other holding up a single sheet of paper marked LIEN. RIGHT person = a CONTRACTOR (a NEW, different character, clearly NOT Carol): a man in a work CAP and a TOOL BELT, plain cream/orange work clothes, pale near-white cream face; he is ALSO ANGRY — brow furrowed, scowling mouth, one hand thrown out or jabbing a finger back toward Carol, arguing BACK at her (NOT apologizing, NOT sheepish). BOTH people are visibly ANGRY and mid-shout — this is a heated TWO-WAY argument, both scowling at each other. Between them on the ground is the abandoned half-finished repair: a leaning step LADDER and an open PAINT CAN with a brush. Keep the cornflower-blue background BEHIND them completely PLAIN and EMPTY — NO wall, NO gray patch, NO paint patch, nothing on the background. "$STYLE" One short caps word LIEN is allowed on the paper Carol holds; keep letters clean and legible; no other text anywhere. EXACTLY TWO people in the whole image (Carol on the left, the contractor on the right) — no clone, no third person, no duplicate, no reflection; each person has exactly one head and two arms." | \
